    "text": "Trajectories from the same input task can vary due to stochasticity in agents, operations, and initialization, resulting in a distribution over possible trajectories rather than a single deterministic behavior.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "For long-horizon tasks with sparse rewards and high partial observability, explicit memory and planning mechanisms outperform purely reactive policies that rely only on recent sensor inputs.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "A proactive memory agent maintains a structured memory bank, updates it with recent trajectory data, and selectively injects memory-grounded reminders to guide the action agent's decisions.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "Reactive policies that map sensor inputs directly to actions can succeed in partially observable environments when the optimal behavior depends on a short history, but they fail when actions depend on events occurring far in the past.",
    "topic": "memory"
  },
  {
    "text": "Optimizing long-horizon tasks is impractical for manual review because episodes can span thousands of steps, and memory errors may remain hidden for extended periods before affecting outcomes.",
    "topic": "memory"
  }
